    idm: ['Flat, shovel-shaped head with evenly rounded lobes and the eyes at the lobe tips ^1,2,3', 'Smallest of the hammerheads ^2', 'Gray to gray-brown or tan, sometimes greenish, paler on the belly; small dark spots may show on the back and sides ^2,3', 'Mature males grow a bulge at the front of the head; females stay evenly rounded ^2,3'],
    sz: 'Most are 3–4 ft, up to about 5 ft. Females run larger. Heaviest on record about 24 lb. ^2,3',
